      "id": "the-locator-pattern",
      "title": "PATTERN-008: The LOCATOR Pattern",
      "category": "Prompt Patterns",
      "description": "An answer with a section number attached feels like proof, right up to the moment you open the section and find it is about notice periods. A citation you never open is just an answer in better clothes, and a wrong one costs more than none because it spends the doubt you would otherwise have kept. 17 prompts for making every claim carry the exact line it rests on, plus the passes that catch a quote sitting near a claim instead of under it. Built on one rule: authorise the absence, or the answer will manufacture a presence.",
